--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (1): Stars with only one observation were put in the table even though the
     RMS scatter is not defined. They can be distinguished by DeltaT=0.
Note (2): Comments on stars with companion orbit or linears trends:
     L: velocity varies linearly with time (see table4.dat)
    CO: a companion and its orbit were found
     C: a published companion exists but an orbit is not given here
     A: the star is chromospherically active based on the emission
        reversal seen at the Ca II H&K lines in our spectrum
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

